WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.034 --> 00:00:02.034
-Hey!
Oh, you look great.

00:00:02.034 --> 00:00:03.803
-Hi!
You look great, too.

00:00:03.803 --> 00:00:05.137
-Thank you so much for coming --

00:00:05.137 --> 00:00:06.739
Oh, thank you very much.
Please.

00:00:06.739 --> 00:00:09.142
For coming back
to "The Tonight Show."

00:00:09.142 --> 00:00:12.778
It's so nice to see you.
I want to see you in person.

00:00:12.778 --> 00:00:16.248
How's your quarantine
experience been, overall?

00:00:16.248 --> 00:00:17.916
-You know,
when quarantine started,

00:00:17.916 --> 00:00:20.052
I was like, "This is it."

00:00:20.052 --> 00:00:21.787
I was made for this life.
-Wow.

00:00:21.787 --> 00:00:24.423
-I didn't have to make up
excuses to not go to things.

00:00:24.423 --> 00:00:26.725
You know, I'm like --
And I got to spend all this time

00:00:26.725 --> 00:00:29.429
with my dogs,
and then after about two weeks,

00:00:29.429 --> 00:00:31.330
I was like, "Oh,
I wasn't made for this life."

00:00:31.330 --> 00:00:32.665
-[ Laughs ]
-I actually need

00:00:32.665 --> 00:00:33.966
human connection.

00:00:33.966 --> 00:00:36.836
And it made me realize
I need to call my mom more.

00:00:36.836 --> 00:00:38.538
I need to check in
with my friends more,

00:00:38.538 --> 00:00:40.206
not just check their Instagram
and be like,

00:00:40.206 --> 00:00:41.907
"Oh, they're on a beach.
They seem fine."

00:00:41.907 --> 00:00:43.343
-[ Laughs ]
It's like, "Really call them..."

00:00:43.343 --> 00:00:45.111
-Call them and talk to people.
-...and say, "How are you?"

00:00:45.111 --> 00:00:47.347
I found it to be
a great bonding experience.

00:00:47.347 --> 00:00:48.982
I'm closer
to all of my friends now.

00:00:48.982 --> 00:00:50.850
I'm closer with everyone
in my life,

00:00:50.850 --> 00:00:53.319
and I am so blessed for that.

00:00:53.319 --> 00:00:57.323
-You were finally, recently,
able to get back to work.

00:00:57.323 --> 00:01:01.361
You just finished filming
a movie with Morgan Freeman.

00:01:01.361 --> 00:01:03.262
How did it feel
to get back on set?

00:01:03.262 --> 00:01:04.830
Was it --
Were you rusty?

00:01:04.830 --> 00:01:06.933
Was it like --
just like riding a bike?

00:01:06.933 --> 00:01:09.202
-I -- There was that moment
where I was like,

00:01:09.202 --> 00:01:10.836
"Do I even know
how to act anymore?"

00:01:10.836 --> 00:01:12.939
-[ Laughing ] Yeah.
-But I got there,

00:01:12.939 --> 00:01:15.341
and it was such a perfect film
to transition

00:01:15.341 --> 00:01:18.611
back into working again after
not really talking to people

00:01:18.611 --> 00:01:21.114
for so long and
not having that kind of

00:01:21.114 --> 00:01:22.548
connection and being on set.

00:01:22.548 --> 00:01:26.686
-Speaking of Morgan Freeman,
you got to take away

00:01:26.686 --> 00:01:29.522
a little souvenir of sorts
from Morgan.

00:01:29.522 --> 00:01:31.157
Can you tell us about that?
And, by the way,

00:01:31.157 --> 00:01:32.925
I'm already jealous,
'cause I know what it is.

00:01:32.925 --> 00:01:34.827
-Yeah. Like, so I'm working
with Morgan Freeman.

00:01:34.827 --> 00:01:36.896
He's one of my idols.
He's an amazing actor.

00:01:36.896 --> 00:01:38.931
He's on that list of people
you want to work with --

00:01:38.931 --> 00:01:41.267
right? -- as an actor.
And it was an amazing time,

00:01:41.267 --> 00:01:43.869
but I did --
I couldn't stop myself

00:01:43.869 --> 00:01:46.572
from asking him
to record my voicemail.

00:01:46.572 --> 00:01:50.310
So now when people call me,
they get to hear Morgan Freeman.

00:01:50.310 --> 00:01:53.512
-And you are the coolest 'cause
you sent us the recording.

00:01:53.512 --> 00:01:56.115
Let's listen to this.

00:01:56.115 --> 00:01:57.717
-You've reached Ruby Rose.

00:01:57.717 --> 00:02:01.354
Leave a number.
Maybe she'll call you back.

00:02:01.354 --> 00:02:03.189
[ Both laugh ]
-"Maybe"?

00:02:03.189 --> 00:02:05.591
Maybe she'll call you back.
-Maybe she'll call you back.

00:02:05.591 --> 00:02:08.027
Oh, my --
That's --

00:02:08.027 --> 00:02:10.062
That's it
for the rest of your life.

00:02:10.062 --> 00:02:11.830
-That's it.
It will never change.

00:02:11.830 --> 00:02:14.367
-No. Why should it change?
That's unbelievable.

00:02:14.367 --> 00:02:16.169
That is -- I love that
you brought it to us.

00:02:16.169 --> 00:02:17.470
Thank you so much.

00:02:17.470 --> 00:02:19.438
And good on Morgan Freeman
for being a good sport.

00:02:19.438 --> 00:02:20.773
You know,
the last time you were here,

00:02:20.773 --> 00:02:23.575
you were here to promote
the first season of "Batwoman,"

00:02:23.575 --> 00:02:25.211
and we were both excited.

00:02:25.211 --> 00:02:27.313
You were Batwoman,
the first one.

00:02:27.313 --> 00:02:30.916
And we were freaking out, but
now you're not Batwoman anymore.

00:02:30.916 --> 00:02:32.952
You -- What happened?

00:02:32.952 --> 00:02:36.255
Why did you leave
after one season?

00:02:36.255 --> 00:02:38.858
-Well, I didn't just leave.
I didn't up and leave.

00:02:38.858 --> 00:02:41.927
We were in such a weird position
because we had to shut down

00:02:41.927 --> 00:02:44.463
before we could finish
the season, because of COVID,

00:02:44.463 --> 00:02:47.433
and then we went into lockdown.

00:02:47.433 --> 00:02:50.102
And there was a lot of,
like I said earlier,

00:02:50.102 --> 00:02:52.805
with reflection and things like
in quarantine and thinking,

00:02:52.805 --> 00:02:55.174
and I ended talking
to Warner Brothers and Greg

00:02:55.174 --> 00:02:58.277
and where the show was going,
and we really just kind of

00:02:58.277 --> 00:03:01.147
had a really honest,
good chat where we sort of

00:03:01.147 --> 00:03:05.518
mutually agreed that Kate Kane
and her story and everything,

00:03:05.518 --> 00:03:07.053
we had done
what we set out to do.

00:03:07.053 --> 00:03:09.021
We achieved --
I'm so proud of what we did.

00:03:09.021 --> 00:03:10.523
I had so much fun.
I mean, you know,

00:03:10.523 --> 00:03:13.025
I cried on your show
because of how excited I was.

00:03:13.025 --> 00:03:16.028
-You were great.
-And I had a blast.

00:03:16.028 --> 00:03:19.499
And I do really feel like
it was right for the show

00:03:19.499 --> 00:03:21.467
to pass the mantle on
to someone else now.

00:03:21.467 --> 00:03:23.236
There's gonna be
many iterations of Batwoman,

00:03:23.236 --> 00:03:26.572
and I'm really proud of it, and
I can't wait to watch season 2.

00:03:26.572 --> 00:03:28.707
-Oh, good.
That's good to hear.

00:03:28.707 --> 00:03:30.943
Well, you crushed on it.

00:03:30.943 --> 00:03:34.180
And it probably was good
training for "The Doorman,"

00:03:34.180 --> 00:03:38.351
because, man,
you kicked butt in this film.

00:03:38.351 --> 00:03:40.920
You shot this film in Romania.

00:03:40.920 --> 00:03:44.890
Did you go to -- Did you see
Dracula's castle at all?

00:03:44.890 --> 00:03:48.094
-Okay, yes. But here's the thing
about Dracula's castle.

00:03:48.094 --> 00:03:51.464
People told me
it was Romania's Disneyland.

00:03:51.464 --> 00:03:53.599
So I'm like, "Let's do this."

00:03:53.599 --> 00:03:56.269
And when I get there,
there's all these merch stands,

00:03:56.269 --> 00:03:58.104
and I had friends that were
like, "Send me back something

00:03:58.104 --> 00:04:00.405
from Dracula's castle,
T-shirts, whatever."

00:04:00.405 --> 00:04:01.974
I buy out everything.

00:04:01.974 --> 00:04:05.378
Then I put the T-shirt on,
it's like Dracula, you know.

00:04:05.378 --> 00:04:07.947
And I go in and I get
a major history lesson

00:04:07.947 --> 00:04:10.316
that this has got
nothing to do with Dracula.

00:04:10.316 --> 00:04:12.351
Like, this is just 'cause
it looks like --

00:04:12.351 --> 00:04:14.954
it's the only castle that fits
the description from the book,

00:04:14.954 --> 00:04:16.522
so they just kind of
made it a thing.

00:04:16.522 --> 00:04:20.759
And I go in and find out this
place was Vlad the Impaler,

00:04:20.759 --> 00:04:24.563
this horrible ruler
who did brutal war crimes,

00:04:24.563 --> 00:04:28.433
and he actually would like
to impale people

00:04:28.433 --> 00:04:31.236
and leave them around the city
and outside the building.

00:04:31.236 --> 00:04:32.505
I'm in there thinking,

00:04:32.505 --> 00:04:35.207
"Is this the right thing
to send home to my family?"

00:04:35.207 --> 00:04:37.910
-[ Laughs ]
No, you can't do that.

00:04:37.910 --> 00:04:39.445
You can't --
No, you can't buy --

00:04:39.445 --> 00:04:41.380
You can't wear that T-shirt.
No, you got to --

00:04:41.380 --> 00:04:43.316
-You can't.
This would be like --

00:04:43.316 --> 00:04:45.785
If it's Disney Land,
it'd be like if Mickey Mouse

00:04:45.785 --> 00:04:47.886
secretly loved hunting people.
-[ Laughs ]

00:04:47.886 --> 00:04:49.488
-And, like, I haven't seen
Minnie Mouse in a while.

00:04:49.488 --> 00:04:50.923
Have you?
-Okay, yeah, yeah.

00:04:50.923 --> 00:04:53.225
-I haven't here in a hot second.
-That's interesting, you know?

00:04:53.225 --> 00:04:54.494
That's interesting.

00:04:54.494 --> 00:04:56.795
Yeah, you don't really
want the merch for that.

00:04:56.795 --> 00:04:59.832
Yeah, you don't think
about that at all.

00:04:59.832 --> 00:05:02.735
"The Doorman,"
Let's talk about your movie.

00:05:02.735 --> 00:05:05.038
"The Doorman,"
it's an action thriller.

00:05:05.038 --> 00:05:09.508
It's fun.
Tell everyone what it's about.

00:05:09.508 --> 00:05:13.212
-Basically it's about Ali,
who's the character that I play.

00:05:13.212 --> 00:05:15.348
She is an ex-Marine,
and she goes through

00:05:15.348 --> 00:05:18.684
a very traumatic experience
at the beginning of the film,

00:05:18.684 --> 00:05:22.421
and she ends up moving back to
New York to restart her life,

00:05:22.421 --> 00:05:25.958
heal, and try to get, you know,
herself back on track.

00:05:25.958 --> 00:05:28.126
And she ends up getting a job
as a doorman,

00:05:28.126 --> 00:05:30.996
which seems like a reasonable,
easy enough job

00:05:30.996 --> 00:05:33.933
to go back into the workplace.

00:05:33.933 --> 00:05:35.368
Unfortunately, she does end up

00:05:35.368 --> 00:05:38.003
being at the wrong place
at the wrong time.

00:05:38.003 --> 00:05:40.139
They end up shutting down
the place that she's working,

00:05:40.139 --> 00:05:42.841
the building, to renovate,
and it actually doubles

00:05:42.841 --> 00:05:46.745
as, really, a robbery, headed by
the one and only Jean Reno.

00:05:46.745 --> 00:05:50.449
And she's there and left
protecting the very few people

00:05:50.449 --> 00:05:53.319
that stayed during
the renovation shutdown.

00:05:53.319 --> 00:05:56.756
And she ends up having
to go from being a doorman

00:05:56.756 --> 00:05:59.158
straight back into being
the trained person

00:05:59.158 --> 00:06:02.661
that she was and saving the day,
or trying to.

00:06:02.661 --> 00:06:04.030
-I want to show a clip.

00:06:04.030 --> 00:06:06.132
Here's Ruby Rose
in "The Doorman."

00:06:06.132 --> 00:06:07.733
Take a look.

00:06:07.733 --> 00:06:10.769
-Why would a decorated officer
hole up here as a doorman?

00:06:10.769 --> 00:06:14.740
-To meet interesting people
like you.

00:06:14.740 --> 00:06:18.711
-I had a friend
that came back after war,

00:06:18.711 --> 00:06:20.379
and he was damaged.

00:06:20.379 --> 00:06:23.749
Are you damaged...Sergeant?

00:06:23.749 --> 00:06:25.350
-[ Chuckles ]

00:06:25.350 --> 00:06:28.087
Not as damaged as you.

00:06:28.087 --> 00:06:32.091
-[ Chuckles ]

00:06:32.091 --> 00:06:33.091
-What about this --

00:06:33.091 --> 00:06:35.528
Unh!
Ohh!

00:06:35.528 --> 00:06:39.198
[ Grunting ]

00:06:39.198 --> 00:06:40.399
Ohh!

00:06:40.399 --> 00:06:45.204
-Get their guns!

00:06:45.204 --> 00:06:46.538
Take the gun.

00:06:46.538 --> 00:06:48.241
Max, give me the rifle.
Find a way out.

00:06:48.241 --> 00:06:50.509
You go that way!

00:06:50.509 --> 00:06:52.978
-Ruby Rose, thanks again
for coming on the show.

00:06:52.978 --> 00:06:54.112
Hope to see you again.

00:06:54.112 --> 00:06:56.249
Stay safe, please.
Ruby Rose, everybody.

